From 2d76d6803adc32b7f672a0fd51bb48d49c02e448 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Williams <213356824+q8itz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:41:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] graphics: retire occlusion queries asynchronously; fix
 multi-wait spin

- A guest occlusion query end no longer submits and waits for the GPU to
  go idle. The result copy stays in the open submission and is written to
  guest memory once that submission's fence signals. GRAW issues 60-900
  queries per frame, and the per-query stall cost 10-80 ms per frame,
  which halved the frame rate and caused long hitches when moving.
- The command processor flushes and polls pending results while the ring
  buffer is idle, so a guest spinning on a result still gets it.
- WaitMultiple no longer truncates its 1 ms poll slice to zero, which made
  every alertable multi-object wait (including the audio worker) busy-spin.
